[{"id":2494133339,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6UqXRb","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?u=e44a465cbebabb9ea2be80b59e6dc07966bef5b7&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","login":"clayjohn","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn"},"body":"Looks great!\r\n\r\nThere are two places where we call `draw(false)`. Both are in editor classes (resource preview and onion skinning). In both cases we are just forcing the rendering server to redraw a viewport without needing to wait for vsync and draw to the main screen. So I don't think either one will regress with this change. In fact, this might be an improvement in both cases as it seems like they wouldn't properly end the frame previously. ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100257#pullrequestreview-2494133339","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100257","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2024-12-11T02:16:13Z"},{"id":2494859576,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6UtIk4","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?u=af70f5d107e9c1447f296643d5a566dab53d25e8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","login":"AThousandShips","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100257#pullrequestreview-2494859576","pull_request_url":"https://api.gi